  "body": "Follow-up of #4338. AGENTS.md \"Commands ship with an MCP tool\".\n\n## What happens\n\nThe holder form (#4338) edits a user holder by its shape: taper, clamp, bore, gauge length, nose diameter and largest diameter. It builds the outline with `holder_library::HolderShape` and lands the edit as one `EditDocumentComponent`. MCP can replace a component with `upsert_tool_component`, but the agent must then send the full outline. MCP has no tool that edits a user holder by its shape fields.\n\n## Expected\n\nAn MCP tool `edit_user_holder` (or a shape option of `upsert_tool_component`) that takes the shape fields, builds the outline with `HolderShape::geometry`, and runs the same `EditDocumentComponent`. A refusal names the value (the `ShapeError` text) or the tool whose fit breaks.\n\n## Done means\n\n- The tool, its row in the `camcraft-mcp` skill, and tests for a change, an undo and a refusal.\n",
